Thank you for the discussion this morning. Attached is the diagnostic readout=
 for circulation.

As agreed, we will first examine the hand-offs to the cost-centre owner at 07=
 and to Japan Finance at 09. The 560 hours observed at those two points are p=
art of the 610 hours of approval waiting in the 38 complete records; the 61% =
in the readout is measured against 1,000 hours of waiting, not the whole rece=
ipt-to-settlement time. We will retain the double check for bank release auth=
orisation at 12.

Before we propose changes, who in Japan Finance should I speak with to confir=
m who is responsible for the current hand-off conditions at 07 and 09? We sho=
uld check the cost-centre and Finance hand-offs separately.

Best,
Nicholas

